      "text": "***********************************************************************\nGottlieb's 2001 (1971)\nTable primary build/scripted by Loserman76, and refreshed by wrd1972\n***********************************************************************\n\n\nFirst, a quick word about \"Loserman\" (Jeff Whitehead). I first met Jeff\nthrough \"VPforums.com\" sometime in 2018 and made him aware that I\ndid a lot of Pinball repair and restoration work as a side hustle. I asked if\nhe would be interested in me providing him resources in the form of\npictures and scans for the many EM machines that went through my\nshop, and the response was absolutely! So, I began to provide countless amounts\nof resources to him to help him create the numerous EM tables that we're familiar\nwith in the Virtual Pinball community.\n\nIt should come as no surprise to anyone the passion that Jeff had for the VP hobby.\nHe will always be known as the VP EM-King as far as I'm concerned, and will likely hold\nthe record for quite some time for the number of EM tables he freely provided to us all\nto enjoy. In short, Jeff was a very talented and invaluable asset to this community.\n\nJeff passed away on November 16th, 2021, and stunned the VP community with his passing. I think\nI can speak for the likely for the lot of us in the VP community, that we will greatly miss\nhim and his passion for this hobby that he helped to make better by his contributions.\n\nIn tribute to Jeff and with permission before his passing, I have refreshed this\nVP10 EM table to add countless new features, and I have tuned it to make it look and play\nas realistically as possible. With the help of the \"VPW\" folks and their\ncontributions, I am confident he would be very proud of how it turned out. May he RIP,\nand now let's play some Pinball in his honor!\n\n,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,